❮ Java Keywords

Thesuperkeyword refers to superclass 
(parent) objects.

It is used to call superclass methods, and to access the superclass 
constructor.

The most common use of thesuperkeyword is to eliminate 
the confusion between superclasses and subclasses that have methods with the 
same name.

To understand thesuperkeyword, you should have a basic understanding ofInheritanceandPolymorphism.

Read more about inheritance (subclasses and superclasses) in ourJava Inheritance Tutorial.

Read more about polymorphism in ourJava Polymorphism Tutorial.

